@startbpmn BP17_MaintainAProject
lang en

output L1 "01_detailed/BP17_MaintainAProject.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP17_MaintainAProject.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - a project has exactly one optional parent: an idea, a goal, a measure, or none: BR-96
'   - the parent is single-valued and the user is never asked what kind of thing it is: BR-96
'   - the kind is declared at creation and there is no migration either way: BR-97, QB-44
'   - a simple project has one board; an activity-based one has a plan: BR-97, BR-101
'   - a project owns one column template, governing every board of that project: BR-108
'   - a project archives directly, carrying its activities and their tasks: BR-23, BR-112
'   - archiving a project is the only way an activity is archived at all: BR-23
'   - archiving withdraws the project from the focus selectables: BR-43
'   - a project deletion takes everything the project is, approve-or-abandon: BR-113, BR-114
'   - the parent survives a project deletion, minus the link: BR-96, BR-114
'   - archived projects are out of the working view: BR-26
'   - the archive is no shield from a deletion: BR-117
'   - unfinished input is a draft, forms included: the field drafts as it is filled in, and the
'     operation that keeps it is drawn ONCE, in BP19, not per editing process. Here it is a
'     bound rule on the step that fills the field: BR-121, SA 2026-10-11
'   - one editor per entity: starting a project and changing one are the same act, so there is
'     one editor node, one submit and one request. Call site BP17.03 (Amend a project) is RETIRED
'     and its id never reused. The template and the board are ENSURED rather than created, so
'     the one chain serves both without a new-or-existing gateway; the kind stays creation-only
'     and the system refuses a change to it: UX-04, DRW-11, BR-97, BR-128, SA 2026-10-14, ADR-066
'   - a step never enumerates the fields a request stores: which fields the entity carries is
'     a Detail Design matter and is not known yet, so the step names the act and its subject
'     only: SA 2026-10-14
'   - the box carries the act's own word, not the generic edit: the user CREATES a project, which
'     the call site's id already said: SA 2026-10-16
'   - NOTHING IS FETCHED HERE. Every record is loaded once, at start-up (BP01), so a step that only
'     went to the store is gone, and one that selects or qualifies what the act works on says so
'     instead of saying read. What a chain still asks the system for is what it COMPUTES, which is
'     business and stays out of the client. When data is read is a detail design decision:
'     BR-128, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-17 ("when we will read data is not a business concern, but a
'     detail design decision ... I rule that this will be done once at startup")
'   - the box carries the act's own word and the branch covers both: the user DEFINES a project,
'     whether it is new or not, as a goal is defined in BP05 and a measure in BP06. One editor per
'     entity serves creating and changing alike: UX-04, BB03, SA 2026-10-16, SA 2026-10-17
'
' Scope: this process is the project as an entity. Laying out and tracking an activity-based
' project's work is BP18, which this process hands over to by opening a project's course.
' Bringing an archived project back is BP15.
'
' Call-site history: the plan was drawn here until 2026-10-10 and moved to BP18 on the Software
' Architect's ruling, so that the project and its plan are one process each. BP17.06 to BP17.13
' are retired and are never reused.
'
' A seam into another process is drawn as one step that asks the system for nothing, with a note
' saying whose business it is, and the hub takes the user back afterwards. DRW-02 makes the seam
' significant, and BP17 and BP09 already drew theirs; the rest of the set did not, which is the
' asymmetry F-3 recorded. Swept on SA 2026-10-16 ("still can't find any checkout action on the
' diagram").
'
' THE KIND IS VERIFIED AT THE WRITE, like every other rule a write binds: the kind is declared once
' and for the project's life, so an edit that would change an existing project's kind is refused with
' its reason and the rest of the edit is stored - the shape BP11.06 uses for a priority change
' outside the Backlog. No surface is trusted to have checked it: BR-97, BR-128, QB-44,
' SA 2026-10-18 (adversarial review).
'
' A NEW PROJECT'S TEMPLATE IS CREATED, NOT CHOSEN. There is no library of templates to select from:
' a template belongs to one project and comes into existence with it, starting from four lanes, one
' per role (BR-108, BR-97). The same write serves a changed project, where there is nothing to give
' it, which is why the step names the new project rather than ensuring anything: BR-108, BR-101,
' BR-111, SA 2026-10-18 ("'Ensure it has a column template' does not make much sense, if there is
' none")
' AND WHAT ITS KIND BRINGS is the one board of a simple project or the empty plan of an
' activity-based one - a plan's boards arrive with its activities, one each (BP18): BR-97, BR-101,
' BR-105, BR-111, SA 2026-10-18 ("What is 'Ensure it has what its kind gives it [...]'?")
'
' Call-site collapsing: creating a simple project and creating an activity-based one are one
' request differing in the kind it carries, and the drawing does NOT dispatch on that kind: the
' board of a simple project and the empty plan of an activity-based one are two permutations of
' one step, discovered at Design. Drawing the gateway was premature, the same call SA made on
' BP06's measure type: BR-97, ADR-069, SA 2026-10-11 ("yes, premature, leave that to detail
' design"), swept 2026-10-16

pool "User" {
  start "Work to organize, or a project to settle"
  :Work a project;
  rule BR-118

  if "What needs doing?" then "start something new, or change what a project is"
    :Define the project;
    rule BR-121
    :Submit the project;
    send "Edit a project" to editIn
    receive "The editing outcome" as created
    note "The parent may be an idea, a goal or a progress measure, or there may be none. The kind holds for the project's life, so it is declared once and is not amendable."
    end "Project recorded"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "plan its work"
    :Open the project's course (BP18);
    note "Laying out the activities and their order is its own process (BP18). A simple project has no plan to open."
    end "Course opened"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "set one aside"
    :Archive a project;
    send "See what archiving a project takes" to archImpactIn
    receive "What the archiving will take" as archImpact
    if "Approve what the archiving takes?" rule BR-112 then "approve"
      :Select a valid cascading option;
      rule BR-19
      :Confirm the archiving;
      send "Archive a project" to archiveIn
      receive "The archiving outcome" as archived
      note "The activities and their tasks go with it. Nothing below a project can be kept behind."
    else "reject"
      end "Archiving abandoned"
    endif
    end "Project set aside"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "end one"
    :Delete a project;
    send "See what deleting a project takes" to delImpactIn
    receive "What the project deletion will take" as delImpact
    if "Approve what the deletion takes?" rule BR-114 then "approve"
      :Select a valid cascading option;
      rule BR-19
      :Confirm the deletion;
      send "Delete a project" to deleteIn
      receive "The deletion outcome" as deleted
    else "reject"
      end "Deletion abandoned"
    endif
    end "Project deleted"
  elseif "What needs doing?" then "look at the archived ones"
    :Open the archived projects (BP15);
    note "The archive is reached by an explicit act, and it holds the activities and tasks that went down with a project. Reading it, bringing one back and destroying one out of it are its own process (BP15)."
    end "Archive opened"
  endif
}

system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Project submitted" as editIn
  call "BP17.02_CreateProject" "Edit a project" {
    if "Does the edit keep the project's kind?" rule BR-97 then "yes"
      :Store the edit;
      rule BR-96
      :Give a new project its own column template;
      rule BR-108
      :Give it what its kind brings: one board where it is simple, an empty plan where it is activity-based;
      rule BR-101
      rule BR-111
    else "no"
      :Store the edit and refuse the kind change, saying why;
      rule BR-97
    endif
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The editing outcome" to created
  note "The new template starts from four columns, one per role. The kind is declared once and never migrates, and the parent is single-valued. A plan orders and tracks; it carries no duration, no float and no critical path."
  end "Project answered"

  messageStart "Archiving impact requested" as archImpactIn
  call "BP17.14_ReadTheProjectArchivingImpact" "See what archiving a project takes" {
    :Report what the archiving will take, and what of it can be declined;
    rule BR-19
    rule BR-113
    rule BR-112
    rule BR-101
  }
  send "What the archiving will take" to archImpact
  note "Archiving a project is the only way an activity is archived at all, and it is approved whole or rejected whole."
  end "Archiving impact answered"

  messageStart "Project archiving requested" as archiveIn
  call "BP17.15_ArchiveProject" "Archive a project" {
    :Archive confirmed items;
    rule BR-23
    rule BR-112
    :Withdraw it from the focus selectables and hide its boards;
    rule BR-43
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The archiving outcome" to archived
  note "An archived project is frozen until it is brought back, and it comes back as the whole bundle it went as."
  end "Project archiving answered"

  messageStart "Project deletion impact requested" as delImpactIn
  call "BP17.04_ReadTheProjectDeletionImpact" "See what deleting a project takes" {
    :Report what the deletion will take, and what of it can be declined;
    rule BR-12
    rule BR-19
    rule BR-113
    rule BR-114
    rule BR-101
    rule BR-117
  }
  send "What the project deletion will take" to delImpact
  note "Everything the project is goes with it. Keeping anything below it is not offered, because nothing below a project can be detached."
  end "Project impact answered"

  messageStart "Project deletion requested" as deleteIn
  call "BP17.05_DeleteProject" "Delete a project" {
    :Delete confirmed items;
    rule BR-108
    rule BR-114
    :Leave the parent standing, minus the link;
    rule BR-96
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The deletion outcome" to deleted
  note "The parent survives a project's deletion. A goal left with no linked idea is flagged on its current state."
  end "Project deletion answered"
}

@endbpmn
